hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of milena masters I  believe that the fastest and most  effective way to grow a business is to  model the strategies of people who've  already done what you're trying to do so  today we're gonna look at how two  friends wanna come in from a middle  class background one coming from  immigrant from Taiwan join forces  believe they could do something great  created a company and eventually sold if  1.65 billion dollars this is a story of  Chad Hurley and Steve Chen from YouTube  and the top three lessons that you can  learn from their success Steve Chen and  Chad Hurley joined forces to build  youtube.com a social video site that  sold to Google for reported 1.65 billion  dollars these two friends met while  working together a PayPal com  they hit it off and would begin spending  a lot of time together discussing their  business ideas however it wasn't until  eBay purchased PayPal for 1.54 billion  that they both would decide to follow  their dreams upon the sale of PayPal the  eBay both China and Hurley would receive  large bonuses they decided to use their  money to create their own venture with  Chinese engineering skills and Hurley's  creativity they thought they had the  right mix to form a company together  they really had no idea about what type  of business to create but felt that  together they could create something  monumental  in January 2005 Hurley and Chen attended  a friend's dinner party in San Francisco  they had taken a few digital videos of  the event and wanted to share them with  each other the next day it could not  find a good way to do it the files were  too big to email and posting them online  would take hours with that Hurley and  China had their first idea for  sustainable business using the money  they had received from the PayPal buyout  Chenin Hurley decided to create YouTube  to make uploading and sharing videos  online as easy as anyone could want  by teaming up and leveraging each  other's strengths and complementing each  other's weaknesses Chen and Hurley were  able to go on to build a company that  itself 1.65 billion dollars to help you  build your company  here are three action items you can  learn from Chen and Hurley action item  number one build an experience many  successful entrepreneurs today are  focusing on not just creating a great  product or service but building an  experience for their customers make it  easy for people to do business with you  and allow them to feel like they are  part of something bigger  they're not just buying from you they're  part of a movement before YouTube came  along online videos were nothing new the  presence on the Internet had been  growing albeit slowly  they were come Watson to upload while  sharing and watches improved even more  difficult few people had the patience or  the desire to wait out the process this  is what Chen and Hurley wanted the  change the experience of people wanted  to share videos with each other they  decided the best way to do this was to  make it easier for people to share what  they wanted to see according to Chen and  Hurley I see her service as one has been  needed for a long time the pieces to  make it all happen just weren't in place  until we came around we needed it to be  a no-brainer  we allowed the community to tell us what  was entertaining them when we started  this company a few years ago we never  expected to be here it's interesting how  the simple idea improving our own video  experience online turned into this  Akshardham number to make the business  unique if you want to send out for your  competitors and compete against the big  brands in your industry you need to find  a way to be unique you have to offer  something different in a creative way  and make potential customers care about  it if you sell the exact same product as  everyone else and provide the exact same  service you're not going to get people  talking and be excited to work with you  Chenin really knew that they had to  create something unique to make people  use their website one of YouTube's major  advantages with that they allowed  everybody to upload videos of themselves  it didn't have to be professionally  edited and they could easily share it  with their friends but made YouTube  unique  was that they made it easier than ever  before to share a quick video of your  mother's birthday or your brother's  wedding you didn't have to be a  technical genius to use their system and  that helped the service go viral  according to Chen and Hurley what our  users want is to watch themselves they  don't want to watch professionally  produced content there are so many  people with cameras that have the  opportunities to create their own  content and so many more people with  editing tools to tell their stories we  feel this is just a tip of the iceberg  we're building a community and we don't  want to bombard people with advertising  action item number three focus on the  customer if you focus on your customer  they'll take care of your business  success get close to them understand  what they really need and get their  feedback on what you can do to be better  businesses that form around customer  problems are more likely to succeed and  are more likely to adopt changes when  the economy dips from day one of YouTube  Hurley and Chen have reaffirmed their  commitment to creating the best possible  service for their customers even when  that came at the expense of the revenues  they are not simply compassion  businessman how to make people happy  instead of making a dollar instead they  see user satisfaction as necessary for  long-term success they believe that  every successful business must start and  listen to their customers and focus on  the customers wants according to Chen  and Hurley if we wanted to we could have  instantly turned this into a ten million  dollar in revenue business per month are  running pre-rolls on the videos but at  that same time we're going to make sure  that whatever revenue model we've built  is going to be something that's accepted  by the users we're not in a hurry we're  interested in building our community  we're trying to improve discovery we're  trying to improve the experience for  people on our site  so remember build an experience make the  company unique and focus on the customer  to finish up this video I wanted to  share one of my favorite true stories  about the YouTube guys and some of their  best quotes after the dinner party that  gave Chen and Hurley the business idea  for YouTube they wanted a simple way to  share their videos of the night so they  immediately went to work on creating the  answer they witnessed a massive growth  of sites such as MySpace I wondered how  they could leverage that growth to their  advantage instead of building their own  social networking site Hurley and Chyna  wanted to take advantage of those that  were already out there to that end they  made it easy for members of those sites  to embed YouTube videos on their pages  they work with those companies that were  already out there instead of trying to  go against them by following this  strategy Chenin Hurley found it easier  to build upon their idea and her company  began to take off  thank you for joining me for another  edition of all in the masters if you  like the video and you want to see more  please give it a thumbs up below I'd  also love to hear what you have to think  about the video if you liked it or if  you didn't like it leave a comment  underneath the video and we'll see you  on the next episode  you
 

